course: dictionary
lesson: 6479
title: Naughty, or just scared?
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Naughty describes a child or pet that behaves badly or does not do what it is told. Read the words around it to be sure. «Little terror» is a joke for a very naughty child, so the word «terror» tells you the child is causing trouble.
explain: Context can also show you that a word does not always fit. «Little children screaming at jabs aren't being naughty, and a calm older brother or sister holding their hand can really help.» They are scared, not behaving badly, so screaming at a jab is not naughty.
explain: The tone of a sentence changes the meaning. «Cheeky monkey» means a naughty child, and it is said fondly, which means with love and a smile. Ask yourself: is this said as a joke, with love, or to be unkind? The clues will tell you.
fact: Naughty means behaving badly, or not doing what you are told. It can describe children and pets.
fact: The comparative forms are naughtier and naughtiest, as in «a naughtier puppy» and «the naughtiest puppy in the house».
fact: «Naughty or nice» is a well-known idea: Santa's list sorts children into those who behaved well and those who did not.
fact: «Little terror» and «cheeky monkey» are said as jokes or with affection, so they are not serious insults.
fact: Naughty can also mean a bit rude or not proper, said in a joking way.
exercise: «Little children screaming at jabs aren't being naughty.» What does this sentence tell you? | Jabs are fun for children | *Crying at a jab is not bad behaviour, because they are scared | Children who scream should be sent to the naughty step | Crying at a jab is always very naughty
exercise: «Little terror» means a very naughty child. What does naughty mean here? | Sitting very still and quiet | Very tired and sleepy | *Behaving badly | Being very kind and helpful
exercise: «Cheeky monkey» is said fondly. What does fondly tell you? | It is said in a whisper | *It is said with love and a smile | It is said by a stranger who is afraid | It is said with anger
test: Which is the correct form for comparing two naughty puppies? | more naughtyer | *naughtier | naughtiest | naughtyer
test: «Little terror» is said as a joke. What does it mean? | A very brave knight | A very kind teacher | *A very naughty child | A very tidy room
exam: Should you call a child who cries at a jab naughty? | No, because crying is always good | Yes, because jabs are fun | *No, they are scared, and naughty means behaving badly | Yes, all crying children are naughty
